WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.940
Television is great for telling serialized
stories over a long period of time, but not

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.440
every TV series is meant to last.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.330
Whether it's because of stiff competition,
upheaval at the network, or simply being ahead

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.790
of their time, some shows are canceled before
they have a chance to reach their full potential.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.500
None of these series made it past a single
season - and we still aren't over it.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Clone High

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.679
The animated MTV show Clone High followed
clones of Abraham Lincoln, JFK, Cleopatra,

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:31.029
and Gandhi, among other famous historical
figures, each reinvented as a different teenage

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.390
archetype, as they try to manage hormones,
homework, and a secret government program

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.660
with evil designs on their school.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.030
"Jeez Abe, you grew like a foot."

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.040
"You grew like, a pair of bewbs."

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.000
The show's irreverent humor and use of real-life
historical figures were bound to lead to controversy,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.080
and its depiction of Gandhi as a horny party
animal led hundreds of Indian citizens to

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.010
go on a hunger strike in protest.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:57.950
After the controversy, the show was ultimately
canceled with no hope of renewal.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.660
Still, while it ended too soon for many fans,
the show's single season remains a fascinating

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.380
time capsule of early-2000s MTV animation.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.960
My So-Called Life

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.009
Following Claire Danes' character Angela Chase
and her friends as they dealt with real, timely

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:17.090
issues like homophobia and abuse, My So-Called
Life's depiction of teenage life was genuinely

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.090
groundbreaking.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.200
From great dialogue to well-written characters,
the show established a unique depiction of

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.469
a high schooler's search for identity.

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:28.469
Danes' performance was sometimes uncomfortably
familiar, and the show's unflinching look

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:31.869
at the less-discussed aspects of adolescence
was a critical hit.

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:33.049
"He's bisexual."

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:35.179
"How can he be bi-anything?

00:01:35.179 --> 00:01:37.689
He's a child, he's obviously very confused."

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:39.520
"No, he's not confused."

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.000
"He wears eyeliner!"

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.770
Unfortunately, while the show was beloved
by its fans, Danes was ready to move on to

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.529
new things by the end of the first season,
and low ratings meant the show was unlikely

00:01:48.529 --> 00:01:50.759
to get a second season with or without her.

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:56.270
Still, its influence reverberated through
nearly every high school-set series that followed.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.270
Firefly

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.939
When discussing shows canceled before their
time, it's basically impossible to exclude

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:02.939
Firefly.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:06.749
The show's focus on science fiction adventures
fused with Western sensibilities, combined

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:10.990
with creator Joss Whedon's trademark dialogue,
made a huge impact on fans.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:15.240
Those fans proved it with their now-legendary
campaigns to save the series, which eventually

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.480
resulted in a big-budget movie continuation,
Serenity.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.180
Like any sci-fi series, elements of Firefly
arguably haven't aged well, but it still remains

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.190
a joy to see Zoe and Wash as one of the only
functional couples on the show.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.490
They're as traumatized and cynical as the
rest of the crew, but nonetheless refuse to

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:35.220
let their past define them - just one reason
Firefly's one-season voyage remains the focus

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.340
of a devoted fanbase.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.340
The Tick

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.810
The original live-action The Tick followed
the addle-brained hero and his frustrated

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:46.760
former accountant-turned-super-sidekick Arthur,
using a mix of Seinfeld-style humor and off-brand

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.760
Justice League-type antics to introduce a
host of ridiculous characters.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.930
"My head feels like it's gonna have a baby!"

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.550
The madcap comedic stylings and Patrick Warburton's
booming voice have become almost inseparable

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:05.710
from the DNA of modern comedies, but The Tick
only lasted one season.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.070
While the show's run might've been short,
it was definitely sweet, with a whole host

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:13.140
of ridiculous allies and enemies menacing
our favorite bulging, blue bug.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.110
"Evil never sleeps mister."

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.790
"Oh, leave me alone.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.970
I'm 112 years old, I'm done."

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.940
"Don't be an Adolf Quitler!"

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.530
Although it's great that Amazon resurrected
the property, without Warburton and the rest

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.830
of the original cast on board, the original
Tick's cancellation still feels like a missed

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.970
opportunity.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.150
The Adventures of Brisco County, Jr.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:36.270
Starring the one and only Bruce Campbell as
Brisco, The Adventures of Brisco County, Jr.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:41.050
mixed classic western tropes like train robberies
and corrupt juries with anachronistic technology

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.790
like rockets and projectors.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.791
Much of the charm came from Campbell's distinctive
comic timing and everyman persona, but the

00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:48.910
scripts were surprisingly clever.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:54.380
The show was set in 1893, a full 100 years
before its airing in 1993, which allowed for

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.740
all sorts of Futurama-esque winking at popular
culture filtered through the lens of classic

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.040
genre trappings.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.020
Anyone who loves Campbell's work - or can
simply appreciate a quirky good time - needs

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.160
to see this cult classic.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.160
The Get Down

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.000
Baz Luhrmann's The Get Down was always going
to be subject to scrutiny.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.880
Luhrmann is a love-him-or-hate-him director,
and when you add in the massive price tag

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.700
and the difficult-to-define genre, the show
was destined to leave some viewers scratching

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:18.700
their heads.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.630
The Get Down tried to tell an unusual kind
of magical realist story about the search

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:27.710
for mythical records, and passionate musical
performances that could convert foe to friend.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.240
Even when the show approached abstraction,
its core trio of kids in the slums of New

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.590
York brought an emotional reality that bedrocked
the series.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.060
"The way I see it, all of us here on this
planet.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.520
And we're on a journey.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.300
And it is a mystery."

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.400
Sadly, the show just never found enough of
an audience, but the entire run is still part

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.970
of the Netflix lineup, just waiting for the
right viewers to get hooked on its musical

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.280
myth.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.490
Freaks and Geeks

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:57.360
Many shows have taken place in high school,
but none with the level of uncomfortable,

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.790
frank honesty that fueled Freaks and Geeks.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:04.430
Brought to viewers by a flock of future famous
faces and writers including Judd Apatow, Seth

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:09.160
Rogen, Linda Cardellini, Jason Segel, and
James Franco, it offered a unique depiction

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.160
of adolescence.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.390
"Yeah well, what are you gonna do?"

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:18.070
"I don't know, what are you gonna do?"

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:21.340
It's stunning to look back on the show and
see the onscreen evolution of some of our

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.040
favorite talent, but even more impressive
is the timelessness of the stories and the

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:26.160
way they're delivered.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:30.550
Although it was set in the early '80s, Freaks
and Geeks remains eternal because of its willingness

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.940
to embrace the awkward, acne-ridden side of
being a teenage misfit.

